      "side": 1,
      "message": "updateCallCapabilities adds CAPABILITY_HOLD when the call is ACTIVE or HOLDING, but doesn\u0027t check whether CAPABILITY_SUPPORT_HOLD is set first.\n   The commit message explains the relationship between the two: CAPABILITY_SUPPORT_HOLD indicates the call can potentially be held, while\n  CAPABILITY_HOLD indicates it can be held right now. Adding CAPABILITY_HOLD without verifying CAPABILITY_SUPPORT_HOLD could set hold capability\n  on connections that don\u0027t actually support holding (e.g., certain call types or BT headsets that don\u0027t advertise three-way calling support).",
      "revId": "25037bf949f0ae23c0ab7d122b99662227ef185f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
